ns mechanical, electrical, plumbing, and controls (MEPC) systems. It also provides professional and consultative services; inspection, troubleshooting, repair, and services; system and/or facility assessments; turnkey rental equipment solutions; MEPC infrastructure solutions; and customized solutions. The company serves research, acute care, and inpatient hospitals; public and private colleges, universities, research centers; entertainment facilities, and amusement rides and parks; data centers; automotive, energy and general manufacturing plants; and life sciences, including organizations and companies, whose work is centered around research and development focused on living things. In addition, it also operates as a mission-critical program management and consulting firm, specializes in the planning, management, and delivery of complex data center infrastructure projects. Limbach Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1901 and is headquartered in Tampa, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael M. McCann | President, CEO & Director | Age 42 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $308K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $20K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Limbach Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $657M market cap on $647M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 18% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $42M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.17\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 16\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 7.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (73% sell ratio, net $2.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 32% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (LMB) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/35/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_LMB_That_Institutions_Follow_111226090601_1794492361.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794492361.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Financial Analysis: Limbach (LMB) versus Its Rivals","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/financial-analysis-limbach-lmb-versus-its-rivals.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794303915.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.754,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Limbach (NASDAQ:LMB) Stock Price Up 12.9% Following Analyst Upgrade","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/limbach-nasdaqlmb-stock-price-up-12-9-following-analyst-upgrade.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794072185.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Wall Street Analysts See a 37.61% Upside in Limbach (LMB): Can the Stock Really Move This High?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025551/wall-street-analysts-see-a-37-61-upside-in-limbach-lmb-can-the-stock-really-move-this-high?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cconsensus_price_target-3025551","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793973302.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Despite Fast-paced Momentum, Limbach (LMB) Is Still a Bargain Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":